# docker/Dockerfile.oap (in the composezao-da-massa superproject) only COPYs
# dependency manifests from this context — package.json, yarn.lock,
# .yarnrc.yml, apps/*/package.json — then runs `yarn install`. App source
# is mounted at runtime, not built into the image.
#
# Without this file Docker ships the whole working tree as the build
# context — most notably .yarn/cache (~240M+) — on every build. Over a
# remote docker context that's a multi-minute upload of bytes the build
# never reads.
#
# Everything excluded below is regenerable (`yarn install` / `next build`)
# or never read by the build. .yarn/releases and .yarnrc.yml are NOT
# excluded — corepack/yarn need them.

# yarn (Berry) — regenerated by `yarn install`
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
.yarn/unplugged

# dependencies / build output
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
out
build
dist
coverage

# vcs / misc
.git
.github
*.log
